[[Hernán Cortés]] built the vault deep in the Gulf ofto store his vast collection of treasures from his travels, including the [[Ring]] of [[Umbra]]. He left dozens of brutal traps around the vault and a guardian Titan, [[Conquistador]] surrounded by a massive force field. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

Following a clue from [[Eathon Lambert]], [[Dante Vale]] found the entrance to the vault during a thunderstorm out in the Sea of Cortés. With help from [[Metagolem]], he entered the vault and used [[Ignatius]] to defend himself from some arrows. He then discovered [[Conquistador]] with the force field. Meanwhile [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Den Fears]] recovered the [[Pied Pipe]] in [[Hamelin Cathedral]]. {{source|Gremlow Infestation!}}

After meeting in Baja, California, the Huntik team dived down to the vault where, following [[Nostradamus]]' quatrain, they used the Pied Pipe to charm Conquistador into disabling the barrier. However they were interrupted by [[Wilder]] and his team, who had found the cave mapped in [[the Organization]]'s extensive data archive. They took them hostage before continuing into the vault, where Dante set of one of the traps, causing a chain reaction and giving the team an opportunity to fight back. Using [[Kaioh the Tracker]], Dante was able to find the Ring from a selection of fake Amulets before regrouping. However, the Organization blocked the exit with rocks, trapping the Huntik team with Conquistador. At the moment, Dante invoked [[Umbra]], teleporting them all to safety. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

